WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:05.139
Look, I've harvested many vegetables today.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.619
Are you going to continue being a farmer?

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.769
If that thing

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:14.900
restrains you with the sense of duty or purpose...

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.109
Ilvia.

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:54.510
(Sils Village 15 years ago)

00:01:57.609 --> 00:01:59.239
(Al's Past)
I've finally dug a full box.

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:03.230
Alright, Al, take a rest first.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:07.299
Since when did you dig so many?

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:10.699
Al? Are they all dug by you alone?

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.159
Yeah, I'm having a good time digging.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.469
Oh, yeah? Good for you.

00:02:18.259 --> 00:02:19.789
Dear?

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.199
How dare you make Al work?

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.659
Mom, you got it wrong.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.599
These botatoes are freshly dug up today. They are for you.
(*A vegetable of another world)

00:02:31.639 --> 00:02:33.469
It's so nice of you.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.689
You have a big harvest.
Is it because your farm land is fertile?

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.050
We really want to get a share of your luck.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:40.370
Stop it!

00:02:41.189 --> 00:02:43.599
I won't let you go by all means today.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.169
Behave yourself.

00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:47.229
Brat, stop it!

00:02:49.039 --> 00:02:49.930
Who is that girl?

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.419
A thief, I guess.

00:02:52.169 --> 00:02:54.289
Why did she steal their vegetables?

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.870
Perhaps she's hungry.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.770
She is either abandoned by her parents or they're dead.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.349
So, she's an orphan?

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.469
Yeah.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.889
Maybe she lives in the mountain nearby.

00:03:08.659 --> 00:03:11.349
Live in the mountain? What will they do to her?

00:03:11.699 --> 00:03:12.909
She's a poor girl,

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:16.099
but it seems that they will hand her to a slave trader.

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:17.159
What?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.719
If she is left alone, she will do bad things again.

00:03:20.009 --> 00:03:21.129
There is nothing we can do about it.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.360
Come with us.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.189
Ouch!

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:33.740
Dang! She ran away!

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.509
Don't let her run! Catch her!

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.349
Hold on!

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.199
I'm not here for the botatoes.
(*A vegetable of another world)

00:03:58.639 --> 00:04:01.800
Botatoes taste bitter if it's eaten raw.

00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:06.419
It's better to peel and make it into soup like this.

00:04:11.699 --> 00:04:13.509
This is made by my mom.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.979
If you don't mind, just eat it.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:17.860
I'm leaving.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.720
Hey!

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.170
Today you'll have omelet rice with tomado.
(A vegetable of another world)

00:04:53.769 --> 00:04:54.959
Hey!

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.550
Today you'll have fish sandwiches.

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:11.860
How does it taste? Is it good?

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.699
The tomado is really yum.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.480
Really? It's grown by me!

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:21.850
You grew it?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:22.810
Yeah!

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.740
My dad said the happiest thing for a farmer

00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:30.069
was to see people enjoy the vegetables he grows.

00:05:30.889 --> 00:05:32.149
It's so true.

00:05:35.019 --> 00:05:37.300
By the way, what's your name?

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:38.660
Ilvia.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.279
I'm Al, Al Wayne.

00:05:41.649 --> 00:05:42.470
Nice to meet you.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:43.670
Al.

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:48.500
Are you hungry?

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.170
No, I'm... Well...

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:04.980
No need.

00:06:05.439 --> 00:06:08.129
If you're hungry, you won't be happy.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:09.560
Eat it.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.339
Thank you, Ilvia.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:20.689
Got you, brat.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.120
You can't escape now.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.850
I must hand you to the slave trader today!

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.160
No!

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.529
Stop it! She has stopped stealing vegetables!

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.029
So, let her go!

00:06:31.259 --> 00:06:32.370
No way!

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.660
Do you know how much loss she has caused us?

00:06:36.019 --> 00:06:38.449
How can we leave her alone?

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.120
Please.

00:06:43.829 --> 00:06:47.110
I'll return the vegetables she stole from you.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.250
Although I can't give you so many vegetables now,

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.509
I'll work really hard

00:06:51.509 --> 00:06:54.579
and grow many vegetables to pay you off.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:55.930
So...

00:06:58.689 --> 00:07:00.860
No way. That's out of the question.

00:07:01.019 --> 00:07:02.370
Piss off.

00:07:02.639 --> 00:07:03.540
Hey!

00:07:05.069 --> 00:07:06.560
What are you doing?

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.170
What has Al done to offend you?

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.689
Wayne-san.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.810
Well, no, actually...

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.209
So that explains it.

00:07:19.019 --> 00:07:21.009
Given the loss she has caused us,

00:07:21.399 --> 00:07:24.930
she can't pay us off even if she is sold to a slave trader.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.310
Oh, I see.

00:07:27.939 --> 00:07:29.050
Well, then.

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:34.589
Take it. This will be the compensation for you.

00:07:35.009 --> 00:07:36.750
Wayne-san!

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:37.959
Isn't it enough?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.509
Yes, yes.

00:07:39.649 --> 00:07:42.069
Since you've already done so, right?

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.069
Since you've said so,

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.680
we'll give in to you.

00:07:47.949 --> 00:07:48.889
Yes.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:54.600
Dad, is it okay to give all the rice to them?

00:07:55.939 --> 00:07:56.980
Yeah.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:01.139
Your mom may kill me though.

00:08:01.269 --> 00:08:02.180
What?

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.870
We'll have to tighten the belt
for the next two months or so.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.509
Dad.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.600
Well, things will work out somehow.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.870
That's quite optimistic.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:20.509
These are...

00:08:21.399 --> 00:08:22.399
You took them away back then.

00:08:24.629 --> 00:08:26.009
Are you returning them?

00:08:27.129 --> 00:08:27.990
Yes.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:35.059
But if we are to turn this basket of botatoes into dishes,

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.309
we'll be short of hands.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.340
Yeah, Dad, you're right.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.620
Ilvia, here!

00:08:50.559 --> 00:08:54.240
We're going to turn these botatoes
into soup bit by bit every day.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.809
Can you help us prepare them?

00:08:57.129 --> 00:08:59.779
Help you prepare? Every day?

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:03.269
Yeah, at our home, every day.

00:09:03.789 --> 00:09:05.690
We'll eat together every day too.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.779
Every day? Together?

00:09:12.649 --> 00:09:13.470
Yeah!

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.470
Let's go. I'm hungry.

00:09:16.659 --> 00:09:17.460
OK!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.500
(Two years later)

00:09:28.919 --> 00:09:31.049
Great! Done!

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.200
Onii-chan.

00:09:35.399 --> 00:09:37.080
I'm done over here too.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:41.220
Let's take a rest and eat something.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.570
No, I'm enjoying myself here.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:44.909
I may as well get it all done.

00:09:45.409 --> 00:09:47.340
Eh?

00:09:47.919 --> 00:09:49.779
But let's still...

00:09:49.809 --> 00:09:50.860
Ilvia.

00:09:51.269 --> 00:09:55.460
Give up. Al was born a farming enthusiast.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.059
You're an idiot.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:01.809
Play with the kids in the village once in a while.

00:10:02.029 --> 00:10:05.179
You don't have to always follow me.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.539
I like being with you.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:10.259
Hey, mind your words.

00:10:11.559 --> 00:10:13.850
Help! Help!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.019
Testa!

00:10:15.019 --> 00:10:16.659
Oh no, they're killer bees.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.049
Are you alright, Testa-kun?

00:10:34.789 --> 00:10:36.980
Thank you so much!

00:10:37.429 --> 00:10:40.379
Lucica-san, you're still as beautiful as always.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.250
Oh my.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.240
Hey, brat!

00:10:44.169 --> 00:10:47.039
How dare you talk like that to my wife?

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:50.330
Even though you're Al's good friend,
I won't show you mercy.

00:10:50.879 --> 00:10:51.919
You got me wrong!

00:10:51.919 --> 00:10:54.240
I was merely expressing my feelings.

00:10:54.289 --> 00:10:55.820
Thank you for your compliment, Testa-kun.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.710
It's a pity that I only like Al!

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:00.740
Eh? What about me?

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:02.120
Oh, right, Al.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.909
We're going to the royal capital.
You must look after our home well.

00:11:06.049 --> 00:11:09.350
Are you going to look for a house again?
Isn't the current house good enough?

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:11.789
We have four people in our family now.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.200
We must find a comfortable place anyway.

00:11:14.629 --> 00:11:15.480
Besides...

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.620
So,

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.269
your mom and I are going out.
I'm leaving the farm work to you.

00:11:21.009 --> 00:11:23.809
I feel the current house is big enough.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.350
We'll bring presents for you.

00:11:28.669 --> 00:11:30.179
Safe journey.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.950
Oh right, Testa.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.720
Why did the killer bees chase you?

00:11:37.169 --> 00:11:39.029
There shouldn't be killer bees nearby.

00:11:39.259 --> 00:11:40.870
Good question.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.879
Look at this.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.179
A map?

00:11:44.529 --> 00:11:47.899
It shows that there is a great treasure
deep in the forest of our village.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:49.059
A treasure?

00:11:49.179 --> 00:11:50.830
Yes, a treasure!

00:11:51.259 --> 00:11:54.409
It's said the forest is dangerous
and people aren't allowed to go there,

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:57.159
but if we avoid the killer bees' nest,

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.539
there will only be monsters as weak as Slimes.

00:12:00.889 --> 00:12:03.909
Let's go there and we'll be back at night.

00:12:05.789 --> 00:12:08.980
We can bring a gem or something to Ilvia-chan.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.289
Oh yeah.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.139
Let's set off now.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.120
OK.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.139
Where are you going? I'm going too.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:18.659
Ilvia, we are going somewhere a bit dangerous.

00:12:18.789 --> 00:12:20.409
You'd better stay home.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.009
I wanna be with you.

00:12:24.309 --> 00:12:26.059
We'll come back at night.

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:27.840
Let's go, Al!

00:12:33.049 --> 00:12:36.960
Why does Ilvia always cling onto me?

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:40.340
She should become friends with the kids in the village.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.320
I guess that's not gonna happen.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:48.039
Ilvia-chan asked me not to tell you about this.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:52.409
Whenever Ilvia-chan is alone, the villagers

00:12:53.299 --> 00:12:54.779
are really mean to her.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.110
Why doesn't she tell me?

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.460
Can it be?

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.720
Ilvia is the reason my parents

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:06.259
are looking for a new home to move into?

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:10.899
Only I have no idea about it.

00:13:11.429 --> 00:13:14.330
Just like you, I can't be of help either.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:18.309
Let's just find the treasure and go back.

00:13:19.129 --> 00:13:20.039
You're right.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:25.940
The map shows it's nearby.

00:13:26.279 --> 00:13:27.870
But all we can see are just rocks.

00:13:32.759 --> 00:13:33.620
What's going on?

00:13:41.289 --> 00:13:42.700
Ouch.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.730
Where are we?

00:13:53.679 --> 00:13:56.570
I didn't expect there to be such a place in the forest.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:58.710
Al.

00:14:00.399 --> 00:14:01.809
There are words here.

00:14:03.409 --> 00:14:04.580
What language is this?

00:14:05.029 --> 00:14:06.610
I can't read this at all.

00:14:17.009 --> 00:14:18.899
What... What's going on?

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.179
Who are you?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.950
Onii-chan! Onii-chan! Onii-chan!

00:14:53.399 --> 00:14:54.690
Onii-chan!

00:14:55.929 --> 00:14:58.409
Onii-chan, you're awake!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.190
Ilvia?

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:04.320
Thank God. You've been unconscious for a while.

00:15:07.129 --> 00:15:09.570
Onii-chan, what's wrong?

00:15:09.919 --> 00:15:13.389
Nothing, I'm fine.

00:15:13.889 --> 00:15:14.649
I'm sorry.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:15.519
Al!

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:17.779
You're awake!

00:15:18.139 --> 00:15:18.929
Testa.

00:15:20.279 --> 00:15:21.370
Where are we?

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.059
Didn't we go into the forest?

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:27.360
Well...

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:38.879
After you fainted,

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:41.309
the volcano erupted all of a sudden.

00:15:42.139 --> 00:15:44.070
The ash buried everything.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.809
The houses and farm land were all buried.

00:15:50.309 --> 00:15:54.179
So, all the villagers came here to take refuge.

00:15:55.539 --> 00:15:56.799
How come?

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:58.830
This is terrible!

00:15:59.799 --> 00:16:04.039
The bridge collapsed. We can't go
to the royal capital, let alone other villages.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.490
Why must this happen?

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:08.639
Testa!

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.690
I found your parents!

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.029
I'll be fine.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:16.789
Al, I'm sorry.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.269
What?

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:29.059
Chief, we can only have so little?

00:16:29.309 --> 00:16:31.799
I'm sorry. This is all that you can get.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:37.370
We've done our best to collect food.
This is all we've got in the village for now.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.590
Please live with it before relief arrives.

00:16:42.289 --> 00:16:44.200
Oh right, what about the farm land?

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:55.450
Damn! It's gone. It's all ruined.

00:17:00.059 --> 00:17:00.960
Onii-chan!

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:03.500
Don't push yourself. Let's go back to the tent.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:08.150
Ilvia, you're hungry, right?

00:17:12.029 --> 00:17:13.109
I'm sorry.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:18.480
Don't say that. It's okay.

00:17:19.079 --> 00:17:20.329
More importantly,

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.400
I don't want you to leave me.

00:17:51.809 --> 00:17:54.079
I'll return the vegetables she stole from you.

00:17:54.559 --> 00:17:57.490
I'll grow many vegetables to pay you off.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.130
My dad said the happiest thing for a farmer

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:05.309
was to see people enjoy the vegetables he grows.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.390
It's so true.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:21.430
So little food for today again.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:24.140
We have seven people in our family.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.440
We'll be starved to death sooner or later.

00:18:33.619 --> 00:18:34.480
Onii-chan.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.250
Ilvia.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.930
Here you are. This is the food for today.

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:42.940
It's more than usual. Why?

00:18:43.809 --> 00:18:45.960
Relief has been sent from the royal capital,

00:18:46.279 --> 00:18:48.619
so we've got more food.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:51.809
Mom and Dad will come back soon.

00:18:52.069 --> 00:18:54.710
Eat more and get better.

00:18:55.289 --> 00:18:57.349
Really? That's great.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.210
You can have your fill too.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:01.150
Yeah!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:04.109
Onii-chan.

00:19:06.369 --> 00:19:10.619
I can't wait to eat the vegetables you grow again.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:15.509
OK, I'll grow vegetables for you.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.019
- Please give us more.
- We can hardly hang on, Chief.

00:19:21.019 --> 00:19:22.089
It'll be good enough if we can get more for the kids.

00:19:22.089 --> 00:19:23.559
Do something.

00:19:23.559 --> 00:19:24.539
There must be more food hidden somewhere.

00:19:24.539 --> 00:19:27.079
Hang in there. Just hang in there.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:53.940
Onii-chan.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.079
I like you best.

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:06.220
Ilvia?

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:08.779
Al!

00:20:09.849 --> 00:20:11.980
It's... Ilvia-chan...

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.109
Ilvia?

00:20:34.039 --> 00:20:36.880
It's already too late when I found her.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:39.819
It's said that she was malnourished.

00:20:41.319 --> 00:20:43.400
How come? How come?

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:46.220
Didn't relief from the royal capital already arrive?

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:47.680
What are you talking about?

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:52.140
Relief? We can't even contact the royal capital at all.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:57.400
How come?

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:05.829
Ilvia!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.960
It's all my fault.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:22.240
It's my fault, Ilvia.

00:21:25.289 --> 00:21:26.359
Now,

00:21:28.690 --> 00:21:31.130
I can let you eat your fill.

